```

## Tab Components

Each tab handles its own data fetching and display:

```tsx
// Traffic Tab - Page views, sessions, referrers
<TrafficTab range={range} />

// AI Tab - LLM usage, tokens, costs
<AITab range={range} />

// Lambda Tab - Invocations, duration, errors
<LambdaTab range={range} />

// Performance Tab - Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
<PerformanceTab range={range} />

// System Tab - Server health, uptime
<SystemTab range={range} />

// Database Tab - Query performance, connections
<DatabaseTab range={range} />

// Users Tab - User activity, registrations
<UsersTab range={range} />
```

**Tab data pattern:**
```tsx
function TrafficTab({ range }: { range: TimeRange }) {
  const { data, isLoading } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ["admin", "traffic", range],
    queryFn: () => fetchTrafficData(range),
    refetchInterval: 60000, // Refresh every minute
  });

  if (isLoading) return <TabSkeleton />;

  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      {/* Stats row */}
      <div className="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <CompactStat label="Page Views" value={data.pageViews} />
        <CompactStat label="Unique Visitors" value={data.uniqueVisitors} />
        <CompactStat label="Avg Session" value={data.avgSession} />
        <CompactStat label="Bounce Rate" value={data.bounceRate} />
      </div>

      {/* Charts */}
      <Card>
        <CardHeader>
          <CardTitle>Traffic Over Time</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent>
          <LineChart data={data.timeSeries} ... />
        </CardContent>
      </Card>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## API Routes

Admin analytics API structure:

```typescript
// /api/admin/analytics - Main analytics endpoint
GET /api/admin/analytics?type=overview&range=24h
GET /api/admin/analytics?type=traffic&range=24h
GET /api/admin/analytics?type=ai&range=24h
GET /api/admin/analytics?type=performance&range=24h

// /api/admin/item-analytics - Per-item analytics
GET /api/admin/item-analytics?id=123&mediaType=movie&range=7d

// /api/admin/errors - Error details
GET /api/admin/errors?type=ServerError&source=api&range=24h
```

## Design Guidelines

1. **Consistent card layout** - Use `Card` with `CardHeader` and `CardContent`
2. **Loading states** - Show skeletons while data fetches
3. **Error handling** - Display error states with retry option
4. **Responsive grids** - Adapt from 1 column (mobile) to 4+ (desktop)
5. **Color coding** - Green for good, yellow for warning, red for critical
6. **Number formatting** - Use `Intl.NumberFormat` for consistency
